    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0286" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1089: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hartman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-26T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>14. Consul Guayaquil cables officials refuse to furnish him information regarding
                    daily deposits. After communicating with Consul request Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs for explanation of refusal.</p>
                <pb facs="0287" n="197" xml:id="pg197"/>
                <p>If daily deposits do not amount to sum provided for in 1908 agreement,<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d160-f1"/> inquire reason of Foreign Office. Cable
                    report:</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d160-f1" n="21" xml:id="d160-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning 1908 agreement, see <ref target="frus1908#pg_273"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1908, pp. 273</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
